Title: Tyneside stories you might have missed this week
Date: 2025-07-13
Firsthand information: {'Speaker': [{'Speaker': 'Artist Charlie Winney', 'Text': 'Artist Charlie Winney said had been "blown away by how huggable it is".', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 6, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 68}}], 'Description': [{'Description': 'A permanent memorial to the Sycamore Gap tree has been unveiled and some of the new Tyne and Wear Metro trains were pulled from service again over air-con leaks.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 1, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 123}}, {'Description': 'People will now be able to touch part of its trunk at the Sill National Landscape Discovery Centre.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 5, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 87}}, {'Description': 'Three of the new Tyne and Wear Metro trains were pulled from service again, as bosses attempt to correct a fault which is causing water to pour into the carriages.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 14, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 137}}, {'Description': 'It was announced TV historian David Olusoga will be among those to receive an honorary degree from Newcastle University this summer.', 'Citation': {'Paragraph': 16, 'StartChar': 0, 'EndChar': 108}}], 'Image': [{'ID': 'image_1', 'Caption': 'Tony Gates sits on a bench next to the trunk. He is clean shaven with short greying hair and is wearing glasses and a pink shirt.'}]}
